# Basic Structs in Go

A struct is a composite data type that groups fields with different names and types. Structs are the primary way Go defines custom data types and models real-world objects.

## Struct Definition

```go
type Person struct {
    Name  string
    Age   int
    Email string
}

type Product struct {
    ID      int
    Name    string
    Price   float64
    InStock bool
}
```

## Creating Struct Instances

```go
// Named field literal
p := Person{
    Name:  "Alice",
    Age:   30,
    Email: "alice@example.com",
}

// Positional literal (order must match)
p2 := Person{"Bob", 25, "bob@example.com"}

// Zero value then assign
var p3 Person
p3.Name = "Charlie"
p3.Age = 35
```

## Accessing Fields with Dot Operator

```go
fmt.Println(p.Name) // Alice
p.Email = "alice@new.com"
fmt.Println(p.Email)
```

## Anonymous Struct

```go
config := struct {
    Host  string
    Port  int
}{
    Host: "localhost",
    Port: 8080,
}
```

## Nested Struct

```go
type Address struct { Street, City, Zip string }
type Person struct {
    Name    string
    Address Address
}
fmt.Println(budi.Address.City)
```

## Struct Comparison

```go
a := Point{1, 2}
b := Point{1, 2}
fmt.Println(a == b) // true
// Structs with slice/map fields cannot use ==
```

starterCode:
package main

import "fmt"

type Address struct {
	Street string
	City   string
	Zip    string
}

type Person struct {
	Name    string
	Age     int
	Address Address
}

type Order struct {
	ID       int
	Customer string
	Items    []string
	Total    float64
	Status   string
}

func main() {
	// Create person with nested address
	budi := Person{
		Name: "Budi Santoso",
		Age:  28,
		Address: Address{
			Street: "Jl. Merdeka No. 17",
			City:   "Jakarta",
			Zip:    "10110",
		},
	}

	fmt.Printf("Name: %s\n", budi.Name)
	fmt.Printf("City: %s\n", budi.Address.City)

	// Anonymous struct
	config := struct {
		Host  string
		Port  int
		Debug bool
	}{
		Host:  "localhost",
		Port:  8080,
		Debug: true,
	}
	fmt.Printf("Server: %s:%d (debug=%v)\n", config.Host, config.Port, config.Debug)

	// Struct comparison
	type Point struct{ X, Y int }
	p1 := Point{1, 2}
	p2 := Point{1, 2}
	p3 := Point{3, 4}
	fmt.Println("p1 == p2:", p1 == p2)
	fmt.Println("p1 == p3:", p1 == p3)

	// Order with items
	order := Order{
		ID:       1001,
		Customer: "Alice",
		Items:    []string{"Laptop", "Mouse", "Keyboard"},
		Total:    15_500_000,
		Status:   "confirmed",
	}
	fmt.Printf("Order #%d: %d items, Total: Rp %.0f\n",
		order.ID, len(order.Items), order.Total)
}
